<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish Permanent silent on acquisition talk.</title>
<headline>Irish Permanent silent on acquisition talk.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish Permanent declined to comment on a newspaper report on Tuesday that it was close to acquiring the London operation of state-owned French bank Credit Foncier de France.</p>
<p>The Irish Independent reported that Irish Permanent was close to completing the purchase of the centralised mortgage lending operation which is believed to have loans of around 200 million pounds outstanding.</p>
<p>The acquisition, though small by the standards of previous acquisitions, would be important strategically, giving Irish Permanent a toehold in the British market, the report said.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
